HEAD:loop/items/AI4DEV-57/gate2-kimi-sql.incomplete-run.txt:526:  Let me also double check finding 2's reachability: does `complete_signup`'s insert of p_ip fail the whole transaction on bad inet? p_ip arrives as text through JSON → PostgREST casts to inet at function invocation, actually! The parameter is `inet`; PostgREST casts the JSON string to inet BEFORE the function body runs. An invalid inet string → error 22P02 at cast time → 400 → no writes at all. So the atomicity isn't even exercised; signup just fails. Still the availability/robustness point stands (garbage header → cannot complete signup, error message leaks raw cast error). And forged-but-valid IP stands regardless.
